# CSA Loom — loom-trino JVM flags.
#
# This is the upstream Trino recommended `etc/jvm.config` (trino.io/docs/current/
# installation/deployment.html, verified 2026-07-28), with ONE deliberate
# deviation: heap is pinned with an explicit -Xmx instead of
# InitialRAMPercentage/MaxRAMPercentage, so the container memory request in
# loom-trino-aca.bicep (4Gi) and the JVM heap (2G) can never drift apart. An
# explicit -Xmx overrides the percentage flags anyway, so carrying both would be
# misleading.
#
# ROUND-2 FIX (#2641): the previous hand-authored list dropped flags the current
# release documents as required. The omissions did NOT fail at boot — they
# surface as a NoClassDefFoundError on real query paths (the missing incubator
# Vector API module) or as pathological recompilation behaviour under load,
# which is worse than a startup failure because /v1/info stays green while
# queries break. The list below is the documented one; do not prune it again.
-server
-Xmx2G
-XX:G1HeapRegionSize=32M
-XX:+ExplicitGCInvokesConcurrent
-XX:+ExitOnOutOfMemoryError
-XX:+HeapDumpOnOutOfMemoryError
-XX:-OmitStackTraceInFastThrow
-XX:ReservedCodeCacheSize=512M
-XX:PerMethodRecompilationCutoff=10000
-XX:PerBytecodeRecompilationCutoff=10000
-Djdk.attach.allowAttachSelf=true
-Djdk.nio.maxCachedBufferSize=2000000
-Dfile.encoding=UTF-8
# Trino's vectorized execution paths load classes from the incubating Vector
# API. Without this the module is not resolvable at runtime and those paths
# throw NoClassDefFoundError mid-query. trinodb/trino:483 ships the 64-bit
# Java 25 runtime this requires (Trino 483 requires Java >= 25.0.1).
--add-modules=jdk.incubator.vector
